==English==

===Etymology===
Tariq Alam Abro was born on April 10, 1958 at Qamber Ali Khan district Larkano, Sindh Pakistan to a school teacher who was known as Master Muhammad Alam Abro he was 11th child. In mid 60s he moved to Hyderabad with him family where his elder brother Dara Alam Abro was working at drawing teacher at Model School Hyderabad. Tariq liver briefly in Liaquat colony but then moved to Sindh University New Campus Jamshoro in 1966. 

He never liked school, in his childhood days he use to escape from school and go to Pakistan National Center library and read what ever he get hold on. 

He started his literary career from a poem, but soon after wrote his first short story “Pavilee” (Quarter) which was published in Soghroo followed by his brake through short story “Peeloo Dhund” (Pale Fog) which was published in Mehran a literary magazine than edited by legendary Imdad Hussani. He wrote 19 television plays for PTV Karachi, He also had a collection of “Tri Siitra” (Haiku) title “ Moorun Uoocha Gaata”.

But the pinnacle of his work is his 1984 novel “ Raahe Gee Wayal Manzara” (Scenes Left Unseen) this novel gave him that leap which pushed him to a undisputed place in modern Sindhi literature. He became a popular among young readers and that popularity grew several folds since.


